A||||5||Eric||cc heads
Z||000000||Eric||05-02-99||11:17 AM||||Does anyone know the cc measurement on the stock 2.8 heads?  I'm gonna throw a stroker kit on the motor and need the measurement in order to find the correct compression pistons.  How would this change when I get the heads done?
Z||000001||theogre||05-03-99||07:19 AM||||even if you knew the starting CC volume of the head, you would need to remeasure the volume after the heads are machined, and the valves installed. Any machine work to the heads will change the combustion chamber volume. there is really no way to predict how much.
Z||000002||Eric||05-03-99||06:16 PM||||It still would be nice to have the numbers.  Just need something to work with.
Z||000003||speed||05-04-99||08:05 PM||||I have just cc my cylinder heads and the value is 56 cc.
Z||000004||Eric||05-04-99||08:22 PM||||Thanks speed.  I assume 56cc is for the stock head, right?
Z||000005||speed||05-05-99||06:32 PM||||Yes, it is for stock heads with the tulip configuration valves(original) if valves have been replace you will have a small change if they have the tulip form but not as deep as the original. If they are flat you will have to substract about 6 cc for the total of the two valves(intake 4 cc, exh. 2 cc).
